# Astro build output (regenerable; served by `astro preview`). Never committed.
dist/

# Astro's generated type/cache dir (content types, env.d.ts shim). Regenerable.
.astro/

# Local npm install of the pinned Astro 6 toolchain. Never committed.
node_modules/

# Vite caches used by Astro's dev server / build.
.vite/

# Lighthouse CI run output (desktop + mobile configs). Regenerated locally
# (npx lhci); never committed.
.lighthouseci/
.lighthouseci-mobile/

# Ralph per-run archives of prd.json + progress.txt at branch/feature transitions.
# These are exact snapshots already recoverable from git history (the prior
# prd.json/progress.txt commits) — keep them on disk for the harness, not in VCS.
scripts/ralph/archive/

# SOURCE audit reports (2026-08-20). The research chapters are WRITTEN FROM
# these documents, but the documents themselves are the raw client deliverable:
# they carry the unredacted evidence (live instance/host identifiers, full
# environment dumps) that the published figures deliberately redact. This repo
# is PUBLIC, so committing one would publish exactly what the redaction removed.
# Keep them beside the repo for reference — like brazalete.jpg, never emitted.
*.docx
*.doc
*.odt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private working material (owner call 2026-08-21, before the first push to a
# PUBLIC GitHub repo). None of it is needed to build or deploy the site — the
# build reads src/, public/ and the four src/data JSONs, and CI runs npm ci +
# scripts/gates + astro build. All of it stays ON DISK; it just stops being
# versioned. NOTE: `git rm --cached` only removes these from the TIP — they
# remain in the 61 commits of existing history, so a public push must start
# from a fresh single commit (see LAUNCH.md) if that history matters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The owner's bracelet reference photo — the header chassis geometry was drawn
# from it (US-902/US-1101). Never emitted to the site; now never versioned.
/brazalete.jpg

# Agent + planning material: the project instruction file, the Ralph PRD, the
# authoring manual and the launch QA record. Internal process, not the product.
/CLAUDE.md
/prd.json
/first-prd-manual.md
/LAUNCH.md

# Local convenience script (build + dev --host).
/host-up.sh

# Per-feature PRDs and archived specs.
/tasks/
/docs/

# The Ralph harness and its verification artifacts (~132 MB, 828 of them PNGs).
# Kept on disk as the per-story proof record; far too heavy — and too internal —
# for a public clone. The committed dev tooling that DOES ship lives one level
# up: scripts/shoot.mjs and scripts/gates/ (the CI gates).
/scripts/ralph/
